From: OHOS SPDK port
Subject: [PATCH] Make unit test environment fixtures independent of libc robust mutexes

The NVMe unit tests already simulate the primary process, device environment,
allocation, and mutex initialization. Also model the two robust mutex calls in
that test environment. These mocks are not linked into the installed libraries
and do not provide or claim runtime robust mutex support on OHOS.
All upstream test registrations and assertions remain intact.

--- a/lib/ut_mock/mock.c
+++ b/lib/ut_mock/mock.c
@@ -5,6 +5,15 @@
 
 #include "spdk_internal/mock.h"
 
+/* Unit fixtures model successful OS calls, just as the existing mutex-init
+ * wrapper does when MOCK_SET is active. These are not runtime replacements
+ * for robust, process-shared mutexes (which some target libcs do not export).
+ * DEFINE_STUB retains MOCK_SET/MOCK_ENQUEUE for explicit error scenarios.
+ */
+DEFINE_STUB(pthread_mutexattr_setrobust, int,
+            (pthread_mutexattr_t *attr, int robustness), 0);
+DEFINE_STUB(pthread_mutex_consistent, int, (pthread_mutex_t *mutex), 0);
+
 DEFINE_WRAPPER(calloc, void *, (size_t nmemb, size_t size), (nmemb, size))
 
 DEFINE_WRAPPER(pthread_mutex_init, int,
